## 1. Security Audit & Vulnerabilities Found

> [!CAUTION]
> The following are **critical security issues** that must be fixed before any production deployment. Several of these could lead to complete system compromise.

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Fix Immediately

| # | Vulnerability | File(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Open Registration Endpoint** | [adminAuth.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#L12-L77) | Anyone can register as an admin via `POST /api/auth/register`. There is **zero access control** — any internet user can create an admin account and gain full system access. |
| 2 | **Admin Routes Without Auth** | [grievance.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/grievance.ts), [feedback.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/feedback.ts) | Routes marked as "admin only" (GET all grievances, PUT/DELETE grievances, GET/PUT/DELETE feedbacks) have **no [authenticateAdmin](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#131-163) middleware**. Anyone can read, modify, or delete all citizen data. |
| 3 | **Hardcoded JWT Fallback Secrets** | [adminAuth.ts:63](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#L63), [simpleAuth.ts:38](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/simpleAuth.ts#L38) | `process.env.JWT_SECRET \|\| "your-secret-key"` and `"fallback-secret"` — if env var is missing, attacker can forge tokens with the default secret. |
| 4 | **Mock Auth Route Left in Codebase** | [mockAuth.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/mockAuth.ts) | Stores passwords in plaintext in memory. Even though not mounted in [index.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/index.ts), it's a code smell and potential risk if accidentally imported. |
| 5 | **Duplicate Route Mounting** | [index.ts:54-55](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/index.ts#L54-L55) | `feedbackRoutes` and `grievanceRoutes` are mounted **twice** each — increases attack surface and causes confusion. |
| 6 | **Error Messages Leak Internal Info** | Multiple route files | Error handlers return `error.message` to clients in non-development mode: `error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Unknown error"`. This leaks stack traces and internal DB error messages. |

### 🟠 HIGH — Fix Before Production

| # | Vulnerability | File(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 7 | **No Rate Limiting** | All routes | No rate limiting on any endpoint. Login can be brute-forced. Public submission endpoints (grievance, feedback) can be spammed. The system will be trivially DDoSable. |
| 8 | **No Helmet / Security Headers** | [index.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/index.ts) | No `helmet` middleware. Missing `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `X-Frame-Options`, CSP, etc. |
| 9 | **Verbose Request Logging in Production** | [index.ts:39-44](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/index.ts#L39-L44) | Logs **all headers and request bodies** to console. This will log passwords, tokens, PII. Must be removed or gated to dev-only. |
| 10 | **No CSRF Protection** | Global | JWT-only auth with no CSRF token for state-changing operations. |
| 11 | **JWT Token Too Long-Lived** | [adminAuth.ts:64](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#L64), [simpleAuth.ts:39](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/simpleAuth.ts#L39) | `24h` and `7d` expiry with **no refresh token mechanism** and **no token revocation**. If a token is compromised, there's no way to invalidate it. |
| 12 | **Password Policy Too Weak** | [adminAuth.ts:16](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#L16) | Only requires `min: 6` characters. No requirement for uppercase, numbers, or special characters. Government systems need strong password policies. |
| 13 | **No Input Sanitization** | Multiple routes | `body("name").notEmpty()` checks presence but doesn't sanitize against XSS payloads stored in DB fields (e.g., `<script>` in grievance description). |
| 14 | **Multiple PrismaClient Instances** | Every route file | Each route file creates `new PrismaClient()` — will exhaust DB connection pool under load. Only [index.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/index.ts) and [officeManagement.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/officeManagement.ts) share the singleton. |
| 15 | **Frontend Stores Token in localStorage** | [AuthContext.tsx:77](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/frontend/src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx#L77) | Vulnerable to XSS — any injected script can steal the admin token. Should use `httpOnly` cookies. |
| 16 | **Console.log Leaks in Frontend API Client** | [api.ts:554-565](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/frontend/src/types/api.ts#L559-L565) | Logs full request details including auth headers and tokens to browser console. |

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Fix for Production Readiness

| # | Issue | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 17 | **No Audit Logging** | No record of who did what, when. Required for government compliance. |
| 18 | **No Data Encryption at Rest** | PII (names, emails, phone numbers, addresses) stored unencrypted. |
| 19 | **No File Upload Validation** | `multer` is installed but file uploads aren't validated for type/content. |
| 20 | **Tracking ID Collision Risk** | [generateTrackingId()](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/grievance.ts#8-14) in grievance.ts uses `Math.random()` — not cryptographically secure, collision possible at scale. |
| 21 | **No Pagination Limit Enforcement** | Some routes accept unbounded `limit` query params — can dump entire tables. |
| 22 | **Dead Code Files** | [simpleAuth.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/simpleAuth.ts), [mockAuth.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/mockAuth.ts), [demo.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/demo.ts), [testAuth.ts](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/testAuth.ts), `*_new.tsx` files — dead code increases attack surface. |
| 23 | **CORS Wildcard Risk** | Multiple hardcoded origins in CORS config. In production, should be strictly limited. |

