## 3. Department System Architecture

### Department Model

```
Department
├── id, name, code (e.g., "POL", "REV", "HLT")
├── description, contactEmail, contactPhone
├── headOfDepartment (reference to Admin)
├── isActive, createdAt, updatedAt
│
├── Admins[] ──── Department admins assigned here
├── SchemeServices[] ──── Services belonging to this dept
├── CertificateServices[]
├── ContactServices[]
├── Grievances[] ──── Grievances routed to this dept
└── Feedbacks[] ──── Feedbacks tagged for this dept
```

### Sample Departments

| Code | Department Name | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `POL` | Police Department | Law enforcement, FIR services, safety |
| `REV` | Revenue Department | Land records, tax, registrations |
| `HLT` | Health Department | Hospitals, vaccination, health schemes |
| `EDU` | Education Department | Schools, scholarships, examinations |
| `PWD` | Public Works Department | Roads, buildings, infrastructure |
| `AGR` | Agriculture Department | Farming schemes, subsidies, crop insurance |
| `SOC` | Social Welfare | Pension, disability, SC/ST/OBC welfare |
| `WRD` | Water Resources Department | Water supply, irrigation |
| `ELC` | Electricity Department | Power supply, billing, connections |
| `TRN` | Transport Department | Licenses, vehicle registration, permits |

### Grievance Routing Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Citizen Submits Grievance] --> B{Department Selected?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Route to Department]
    B -->|No / General| D[Goes to SuperAdmin Queue]
    C --> E[Dept Admin Receives Notification]
    E --> F[Dept Admin Reviews]
    F --> G{Action}
    G -->|Assign| H[Assign to Staff Member]
    G -->|Escalate| I[Escalate to SuperAdmin]
    G -->|Resolve| J[Mark Solved + Notes]
    J --> K[Citizen Gets Status Update]
    D --> L[SuperAdmin Routes to Department]
    L --> C
```

