## 5. Backend Hardening

### 5.1 Immediate Security Fixes

```
Task List:
├── ☐ Remove /api/auth/register from public access (or restrict to SuperAdmin-only)
├── ☐ Add authenticateAdmin to ALL grievance and feedback admin routes
├── ☐ Remove hardcoded JWT fallback secrets — CRASH if JWT_SECRET missing
├── ☐ Delete mockAuth.ts, simpleAuth.ts, testAuth.ts, demo.ts
├── ☐ Fix duplicate route mounting in index.ts
├── ☐ Remove verbose request logging (or gate behind NODE_ENV === 'development')
├── ☐ Stop leaking error.message to clients — return generic error in production
├── ☐ Remove console.log from frontend API client
```

### 5.2 New Middleware Stack

```
Middleware Pipeline (in order):
1. helmet()                           — Security headers
2. cors(strictConfig)                 — Strict origin whitelist
3. express.json({ limit: '1mb' })     — Body size limit
4. rateLimiter (global)               — 100 req/min per IP
5. rateLimiter (auth)                 — 5 login attempts/15min per IP
6. rateLimiter (public submit)        — 10 submissions/hour per IP
7. requestId middleware               — Unique ID per request for tracing
8. structured logger (pino/winston)   — Replace console.log
9. express.urlencoded                 — Form data
10. routes...
11. 404 handler
12. Global error handler (sanitized)
```

### 5.3 Auth Overhaul

```
Changes:
├── Access token: 15 minutes (short-lived)
├── Refresh token: 7 days (httpOnly cookie, rotated on use)
├── Token stored in httpOnly + Secure + SameSite=Strict cookie
├── Session table for revocation (logout = delete session)
├── Account lockout after 5 failed attempts (15 min lockout)
├── Password policy: min 8 chars, 1 upper, 1 lower, 1 number, 1 special
├── bcrypt rounds: 12 (already good)
└── SuperAdmin-only endpoint to create new admins
```

### 5.4 New API Routes

```
Auth Routes:
  POST   /api/auth/login                — Login (returns httpOnly cookie)
  POST   /api/auth/refresh              — Refresh access token
  POST   /api/auth/logout               — Invalidate session
  GET    /api/auth/profile              — Get current admin profile
  PUT    /api/auth/change-password      — Change own password

SuperAdmin Routes:
  POST   /api/admin/create              — Create department admin (SuperAdmin only)
  GET    /api/admin/list                — List all admins
  PUT    /api/admin/:id                 — Update admin
  PATCH  /api/admin/:id/toggle          — Activate/deactivate admin
  DELETE /api/admin/:id                 — Remove admin

Department Routes:
  POST   /api/departments               — Create department (SuperAdmin)
  GET    /api/departments               — List all departments
  GET    /api/departments/:id           — Get department details
  PUT    /api/departments/:id           — Update department (SuperAdmin)
  PATCH  /api/departments/:id/toggle    — Activate/deactivate (SuperAdmin)
  GET    /api/departments/:id/stats     — Department analytics

Audit Routes:
  GET    /api/audit-logs                — View audit trail (SuperAdmin)
  GET    /api/audit-logs/:entity/:id    — View logs for specific entity

Notification Routes:
  GET    /api/notifications             — Get my notifications
  PATCH  /api/notifications/:id/read    — Mark as read
  PATCH  /api/notifications/read-all    — Mark all as read
```

### 5.5 Singleton PrismaClient

```typescript
// backend/lib/prisma.ts — Single shared instance
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";

const globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as { prisma: PrismaClient };

export const prisma =
  globalForPrisma.prisma ||
  new PrismaClient({
    log: process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" 
      ? ["query", "warn", "error"] 
      : ["error"],
  });

if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production") {
  globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma;
}
```

