## 7. Scalability for 4 Million Users

### 7.1 Database Optimization

```
PostgreSQL Tuning:
├── Connection pooling: PgBouncer (min 20, max 100 connections)
├── Read replicas for public-facing queries (services, tracking)
├── Materialized views for analytics/stats dashboards
├── Partitioning: Grievance table by createdAt (monthly partitions)
├── Proper indexes on all frequently-queried columns
├── VACUUM and ANALYZE schedules
└── Query optimization: N+1 query elimination in Prisma

Expected Query Volumes (4M users):
├── Public service views:     ~50,000 req/day
├── Grievance submissions:    ~5,000-10,000/day
├── Feedback submissions:     ~2,000-5,000/day
├── Grievance tracking:       ~20,000 req/day
├── Admin panel (all admins):  ~5,000 req/day
└── Peak multiplier:           3-5x during business hours
```

### 7.2 Caching Strategy

```
Redis Caching Layers:
├── Published services list:    Cache 5 min, invalidate on publish/update
├── Department list:            Cache 1 hour
├── Individual service details: Cache 5 min
├── Grievance tracking lookup:  Cache 1 min
├── Admin session validation:   Cache 5 min
├── Rate limit counters:        Redis-based (not in-memory)
└── Dashboard statistics:       Cache 15 min, background refresh
```

### 7.3 Infrastructure Recommendations

```
Production Architecture:
├── API Server: 2-4 instances behind load balancer (Nginx/ALB)
├── Database: PostgreSQL 15+ with read replica
├── Cache: Redis 7+ (ElastiCache or self-hosted)
├── CDN: CloudFront/Cloudflare for frontend assets
├── File Storage: S3/MinIO for grievance attachments
├── Queue: BullMQ (Redis-backed) for async tasks
│   ├── Email notifications
│   ├── Grievance auto-routing
│   ├── SLA breach alerts
│   └── Report generation
├── Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana
├── Logging: ELK stack or CloudWatch
└── CI/CD: GitHub Actions → Docker → ECR → ECS/EC2
```

### 7.4 API Performance Targets

| Endpoint | Target p95 Latency | Current Risk |
|---|---|---|
| GET /public/list (services) | < 100ms | No caching, N+1 queries |
| POST /grievances | < 200ms | OK, but no rate limit |
| GET /grievances/track/:id | < 50ms | OK with index |
| GET /admin/dashboard | < 300ms | Multiple unoptimized queries |
| POST /auth/login | < 500ms (bcrypt) | No rate limit, brute-forceable |

