## Summary

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Start with Phase 1 (Security Hardening).** The current codebase has vulnerabilities that would allow anyone on the internet to register as an admin and access all citizen data. Nothing else matters until these are fixed.

**Key numbers:**
- **23 vulnerabilities** identified (6 critical, 10 high, 7 medium)
- **6 phases** of work across ~12 weeks
- **~150+ tasks** total
- **10+ new database models/modifications**
- **15+ new API endpoints**
- **10+ new frontend pages**

**The single most important first step:** Lock down the `/api/auth/register` endpoint and add [authenticateAdmin](file:///home/archilect/Information-Service-part2/backend/routes/adminAuth.ts#131-163) to the grievance and feedback admin routes.
